# ShelfSense — Complete Entity Relationship Diagram

## Database Schema (6 Tables)

```mermaid
erDiagram
    USERS {
        INTEGER id PK "AUTO INCREMENT"
        TEXT username "NOT NULL, UNIQUE"
        TEXT email "NOT NULL, UNIQUE"
        TEXT password_hash "NOT NULL"
        TEXT role "DEFAULT 'staff' (staff/admin)"
        DATETIME created_at "DEFAULT NOW()"
    }

    SHELVES {
        INTEGER id PK "AUTO INCREMENT"
        TEXT name "NOT NULL, e.g. 'Aisle 3 - Shelf B'"
        TEXT location "NULLABLE, e.g. 'Store Floor 1'"
        TEXT camera_source "DEFAULT '0' (webcam/RTSP URL)"
        TEXT reference_image "path to empty-shelf photo"
        BOOLEAN is_active "DEFAULT TRUE"
        DATETIME created_at "DEFAULT NOW()"
    }

    ZONES {
        INTEGER id PK "AUTO INCREMENT"
        INTEGER shelf_id FK "NOT NULL"
        TEXT zone_name "NOT NULL"
        TEXT product_name "DEFAULT 'Unassigned'"
        INTEGER x "NOT NULL"
        INTEGER y "NOT NULL"
        INTEGER width "NOT NULL"
        INTEGER height "NOT NULL"
        REAL full_threshold "DEFAULT 0.50"
        REAL low_threshold "DEFAULT 0.15"
        DATETIME created_at "DEFAULT NOW()"
    }

    ANALYSIS_RUNS {
        INTEGER id PK "AUTO INCREMENT"
        INTEGER shelf_id FK "NOT NULL"
        TEXT image_path "the capture that was analysed"
        TEXT status "success / failed"
        DATETIME started_at "NOT NULL"
        DATETIME completed_at "NULLABLE"
    }

    ANALYSIS_RESULTS {
        INTEGER id PK "AUTO INCREMENT"
        INTEGER run_id FK "NOT NULL"
        INTEGER zone_id FK "NOT NULL"
        REAL fill_score "NOT NULL, 0.0-1.0"
        TEXT status "NOT NULL: FULL/LOW/EMPTY"
    }

    ALERTS {
        INTEGER id PK "AUTO INCREMENT"
        INTEGER zone_id FK "NOT NULL"
        INTEGER result_id FK "NOT NULL"
        TEXT alert_type "LOW / EMPTY"
        TEXT severity "warning / critical"
        TEXT message "e.g. 'Zone A is EMPTY - restock needed'"
        BOOLEAN is_sent "DEFAULT FALSE"
        BOOLEAN is_acknowledged "DEFAULT FALSE"
        INTEGER acknowledged_by FK "NULLABLE (user id)"
        DATETIME triggered_at "DEFAULT NOW()"
        DATETIME acknowledged_at "NULLABLE"
    }

    USERS ||--o{ ALERTS : "acknowledges"
    SHELVES ||--o{ ZONES : "has many"
    SHELVES ||--o{ ANALYSIS_RUNS : "has many"
    ZONES ||--o{ ANALYSIS_RESULTS : "has many"
    ZONES ||--o{ ALERTS : "triggers"
    ANALYSIS_RUNS ||--o{ ANALYSIS_RESULTS : "contains"
    ANALYSIS_RESULTS ||--o{ ALERTS : "generates"
```

## Relationships Explained

| Parent | Child | Type | Meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| **shelves** → zones | One-to-Many | One shelf has many zones drawn on it |
| **shelves** → analysis_runs | One-to-Many | Each analysis run targets one shelf |
| **analysis_runs** → analysis_results | One-to-Many | One run produces N results (one per zone) |
| **zones** → analysis_results | One-to-Many | Each zone accumulates results over time |
| **zones** → alerts | One-to-Many | A zone can trigger many alerts over its lifetime |
| **analysis_results** → alerts | One-to-Many | A specific result (e.g. score=0.05, EMPTY) triggers an alert |
| **users** → alerts | One-to-Many | A user can acknowledge many alerts |

## What Each Table Does

### `users` — Who uses the dashboard
Stores staff/admin accounts for the dashboard. Admins can manage zones and shelves; staff can view status and acknowledge alerts.

### `shelves` — Physical shelf units
A shelf is a physical unit in the store with its own camera. It groups zones together and holds the camera source (webcam index or RTSP URL) and the empty reference image.

### `zones` — Regions on a shelf
A rectangular area on a shelf mapped to a product. Previously this was in `zones.json` — now it lives in the DB with a `shelf_id` linking it to its parent shelf.

### `analysis_runs` — "When did we scan?"
Groups results by scan. Instead of each result independently tracking `image_path` and timestamp, the **run** holds that metadata. One run = one camera capture = N results.

### `analysis_results` — "What did we find?"
The occupancy reading for one zone during one run. Contains the fill_score (0.0–1.0) and status (FULL/LOW/EMPTY).

### `alerts` — "What needs attention?"
Created automatically when a zone goes LOW or EMPTY. Tracks:
- **Was it sent?** (email/SMS/webhook sent to staff)
- **Was it acknowledged?** (staff clicked "I'll restock this")
- **Who acknowledged it?** (accountability)
- **Severity**: LOW → `warning`, EMPTY → `critical`

## Data Flow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    U["👤 Admin registers shelves\nand draws zones"] -->|INSERT| S["shelves table"]
    S -->|shelf has zones| Z["zones table"]

    CAM["📷 Camera captures photo"] --> RUN["analysis_runs table\n(new run created)"]
    Z -->|load zone coordinates| CV["🔍 ShelfAnalyzer\nCV Pipeline"]
    RUN --> CV
    CV -->|"INSERT results"| R["analysis_results table\nfill_score + status per zone"]

    R -->|"status = LOW or EMPTY?"| A["alerts table\nalert created automatically"]
    A -->|"is_sent = FALSE?"| N["📧 Notification Service\nsend email/SMS/webhook"]
    N -->|"mark is_sent = TRUE"| A

    A -->|"staff sees alert"| DASH["📊 Dashboard"]
    DASH -->|"staff clicks Acknowledge"| A
    R -->|"latest results"| DASH
    R -->|"historical data"| CHART["📈 Trend Charts"]
```

